3. PROJECT OVERVIEW

BudgetBasics is a responsive educational web application designed to help students and beginners understand personal budgeting and responsible money management.

The application provides simple explanations, visual learning content and interactive tools related to budgeting, saving, spending habits, needs and wants, common money mistakes and financial planning.

BudgetBasics is developed as an educational project. It does not provide banking services, real financial transactions or professional financial advice.


4. PURPOSE OF THE PROJECT

The purpose of BudgetBasics is to make basic financial concepts easier for students to understand through an interactive and user-friendly web application.

The application helps users:

• Understand basic budgeting concepts.
• Identify needs and wants.
• Understand the 50-30-20 budgeting rule.
• Plan and manage sample expenses.
• Set savings goals.
• Learn about common money mistakes.
• Explore financial infographics.
• Ask basic budgeting questions through the chatbot.
• Develop responsible spending and saving habits.


5. MAIN FEATURES

5.1 Budgeting Basics

The Budgeting Basics section provides beginner-friendly information about income, expenses, budgeting, saving and responsible spending habits.


5.2 Needs vs Wants

Users can interact with questions and examples to understand the difference between essential requirements and optional purchases.


5.3 50-30-20 Calculator

The calculator demonstrates the distribution of income according to the 50-30-20 budgeting rule.

The calculated values are provided for educational and demonstration purposes.


5.4 Savings Goals

Users can enter:

• Goal name
• Target amount
• Current savings
• Monthly contribution

The application calculates the remaining amount and provides an estimated number of months required to reach the savings goal.


5.5 Expense Planner

The Expense Planner allows users to manage sample expenses.

Users can:

• Add an expense.
• Select an expense category.
• Enter an expense description.
• Enter an amount.
• Edit an expense.
• Delete an expense.
• Filter expenses by category.
• View total expenses.
• View the remaining budget.


5.6 Money Mistakes

The Money Mistakes section explains common financial mistakes such as unnecessary spending, impulse purchases and poor budgeting habits.


5.7 Learning Gallery

The Learning Gallery provides visual educational content related to budgeting, saving and financial awareness.

Users can filter the displayed content according to topic.


5.8 Educational Chatbot

BudgetBasics includes a basic rule-based educational chatbot.

The chatbot responds to predefined financial questions and keywords.

Example topics include:

• What is a need?
• What is a want?
• How much should I save?
• How can I avoid overspending?
• What is budgeting?

The chatbot provides basic educational information and does not provide professional financial advice.


5.9 Search, Sort and Filter

Learning content can be searched, sorted and filtered to help users find relevant information quickly.


5.10 Feedback and Contact

The application provides a client-side feedback and contact form with validation and confirmation feedback.


5.11 Responsive Design

The application is designed to work on:

• Desktop
• Tablet
• Mobile devices


