9. INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS

Step 1: Extract the Project

Extract the submitted BudgetBasics project ZIP file to a suitable location.


Step 2: Open the Project

Open the extracted BudgetBasics project folder in Visual Studio Code.


Step 3: Open Terminal

Open the integrated terminal in Visual Studio Code.


Step 4: Install Dependencies

Run the following command:

npm install


Step 5: Start the Development Server

Run:

npm run dev


Step 6: Open the Application

After running the command, the terminal will display the local development URL.

Open the displayed URL in a supported web browser.


10. PRODUCTION BUILD

To create a production build, run:

npm run build


If the project supports local production preview, run:

npm run preview


The generated production files will be created according to the project's React build configuration.


11. HOW TO USE THE APPLICATION

1. Start the React development server.
2. Open the local URL shown in the terminal.
3. Navigate through the application.
4. Explore the Budgeting Basics section.
5. Use the Needs vs Wants activity.
6. Enter an amount in the 50-30-20 calculator.
7. Create a sample savings goal.
8. Add sample expenses in the Expense Planner.
9. Explore the Money Mistakes section.
10. Filter the Learning Gallery.
11. Use the educational chatbot.
12. Submit the feedback/contact form using valid information.


