13. ASSUMPTIONS

The following assumptions have been made during the development of the project:

1. The application is intended for educational purposes.
2. Users have access to a modern web browser.
3. Node.js and npm are installed before running the React application.
4. The application does not require a backend server.
5. The application does not require a database.
6. Financial calculations are educational estimates.
7. The chatbot provides predefined educational responses.
8. No real banking or financial transactions are processed.
9. Users should not enter sensitive financial or banking information.
10. The application does not provide professional financial advice.


14. DATA AND PRIVACY

BudgetBasics does not require a server-side database.

The application does not process real financial transactions or banking information.

Users should not enter:

• Bank account numbers
• Credit or debit card numbers
• Passwords
• PINs
• Other sensitive financial information

The application is designed as an educational financial-awareness project.


